From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:54:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(models): preserve optional geometry declarations

Retain modern and legacy geometry declarations that omit texture dimensions
or the bones array. Use the native 64 by 64 texture defaults independently
for each absent or null dimension, and keep a missing bones array as an
empty model without mutating the source JSON.

Upstream PR #2 now owns invisible-cube export, missing UV defaults,
locator-only fitting and source-preserving UV normalization. Keep those
changes and their tests in the upstream base; this remaining patch changes
only the optional-field parser and its targeted regression.
https://github.com/oryxel1/CubeConverter/pull/2

The matching Bedrock 1.26.51.1/protocol 2193 compiler caller supplies width
and height 64. Twelve original bounded texture-dimension controls cover
absent/null fields and independent overrides with two caller defaults.
That reference does not establish schema dispatch, inherited/cached model
dimensions, complete bone loading or native rendering parity.
